From cea47500f58c44a2c75a406b1e164a43cecdd41f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mavis <Mavis@MiniMax.local>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 05:37:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf: eliminate double Haversine calc and add reliability
 cache
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two performance hot-spots identified during code review:

1) StationFilterAndSorterImpl.getStationsNearLocation() was calling
   GeoUtils.calculateDistance() TWICE per station — once in .filter{}
   and once in .sortedBy{}. Haversine = 6 trig operations per call.
   For 100 stations in radius, that was ~1200 unnecessary calls per
   map emission (emission happens 3x during Phase 1 startup).

   Fix: single mapNotNull pass that computes distance once, then
   sortedBy on cached Pair.second. Zero behavior change.

2) PriceReliabilityCalculator was called from multiple places
   (GasStationRepository.logStationStatusSummary, GetBestStationsUseCase)
   and ran Calendar.getInstance() + multiple when-chains on every call.
   For 100 stations x 3 emissions = 300 calls per startup.

   Fix: LRU cache (256 entries, ~100 stations x 2-3 fuel types) keyed
   on (stationId, fuelType, updatedAt, source, sourceCount, hasPhoto,
   available). Cache TTL = 60s (avoids stale ageDays on long sessions).
   Clear via PriceReliabilityCalculator.clearCache() for tests.

Existing tests should pass without modification:
- StationFilterAndSorterTest: signature unchanged
- PriceReliabilityCalculatorTest: same inputs → same outputs (cache is
  transparent)
